<VI _name="lvai_bind_pane_typedef.vi" description="Installs a .ctl typedef onto named FRONT PANEL terminals of an existing CLASS MEMBER\2C through {LV.Control} Replace\2C and saves the VI and its owning class in the same run. Shape copied from scripts/lvai_add_class_method.xml\2C which does the identical Replace with a .lvclass path.\0A\0AWHY IT EXISTS. A GENERATED VI CANNOT CARRY A TYPEDEF ON ITS OWN PANE\3A AIXML has no typedef in its grammar\2C so a control it authored is the bare underlying type\2C and a call into a subVI whose terminal IS the typedef then wears a coercion dot. lvai_bind_typedef_constants repairs the CONSTANT case and finds its target by the constant's LABEL\2C so it cannot reach a front-panel control. This is that other half.\0A\0ATHE CLASS PATH IS REQUIRED\2C AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT\2C NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Measured 2026-09-18 on a plain VI in no project and no class\3A with the class save left out\2C Replace plus Save.Instrument answered error 0 on every stage and the saved file carried ZERO typedef objects - LabVIEW had rewritten it (a VICD block appeared) and dropped the binding. The class Save is what commits it. What commits it for a VI that is not a class member is NOT established\2C so this helper does not pretend to offer that.\0A\0ATERMINALS ARE FOUND BY NAME\2C NEVER BY INDEX. Controls[] order is front-panel creation order for a generated VI and error-clusters-first for a template-built one\2C so an index is not portable. The Case Structure around Search 1D Array is there because it answers -1 for a miss and Index Array then CLAMPS TO ELEMENT 0 - which would silently retype the error cluster instead.\0A\0AAND THE FIRST OPEN OF A VI LABVIEW HAS NEVER LOADED READS EVERY CONTROL NAME AS EMPTY. Measured on the same fixture\2C twice\3A the first run saw four nameless controls and bound nothing at error 0\3B the second saw all four names and bound. So 'terminals bound' must be compared against the number of names asked for\2C and a zero is a reason to retry rather than a verdict.\0A\0AAND THE REPLACE IS A SILENT NO-OP OUTSIDE THE IDE'S OWN APPLICATION INSTANCE\2C so everything opens through Project\3AActive Project -> Application\2C and A PROJECT MUST BE OPEN AND ACTIVE\3A with none open that hop answers Error 1055. Replace's own error is carried out of both structures as an ARRAY\2C one entry per candidate\2C because discarding it is how a failed bind came to report success.">
